From 11bf491b2cbc00ee82d082311f5f55d5e7f94876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work25_heapinfo_rm_prodconfig
 <adbtrr_work25_heapinfo_rm_prodconfig@local>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:13:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configs/rtl8730e: enable the allocation backtrace engine on
 loadable_ext_ddr_st7785

No configuration selected the backtrace engine, so the feature recorded nothing
anywhere. CONFIG_DEBUG_MM_HEAPINFO forces CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE to 3 in
tinyara/mm/mm.h, which reserves the per-node backtrace[] array, but with
CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE unset MM_ADD_BACKTRACE() resolves to the arch
up_backtrace() branch, and with CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_BACKTRACE unset the only
up_backtrace() in the link is the weak stub in mm_backtrace.c, which returns 0
and stores a NULL. Every node therefore paid for the array while "memleak" and
"heapinfo -t" printed an empty call path.

This config already carried the intended settings, but written as
"#CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE=4" and "#CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE=y" - comment lines, not
settings - placed inside a generated section where savedefconfig would drop
them. Replace them with real entries in the positions kconfig emits:

  CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE=y      selects the EHABI unwinder, and turns on
                                -funwind-tables for the user-space pass
  CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE=3         the depth mm.h already forces, stated explicitly
  CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE_SKIP=3    the existing compile-time default

The depth is left at 3 and the sequence number stays off so the node layout is
byte for byte what this configuration already had: allocnode and freenode are
unchanged, and the only cost is the unwind tables in the user image. Raising the
depth or adding the sequence number is a separate decision with a separate RAM
cost.

CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_BACKTRACE stays unset. It is a hidden symbol for an
architecture that provides a real up_backtrace(); amebasmart does not, and the
arch Make.defs says so.

Verified against this defconfig: the user pass now resolves MM_ADD_BACKTRACE()
to sched_backtrace(), the kernel pass to the sequence-number-only form, and both
passes compile.
---
 .../configs/rtl8730e/loadable_ext_ddr_st7785/defconfig | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/configs/rtl8730e/loadable_ext_ddr_st7785/defconfig b/build/configs/rtl8730e/loadable_ext_ddr_st7785/defconfig
index 01a98242..426d5fcd 100644
--- a/build/configs/rtl8730e/loadable_ext_ddr_st7785/defconfig
+++ b/build/configs/rtl8730e/loadable_ext_ddr_st7785/defconfig
@@ -416,10 +416,7 @@ CONFIG_SECURITY_LEVEL=y
 # Kernel Features
 #
 # CONFIG_DISABLE_OS_API is not set
-#CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_BACKTRACE=y
-#CONFIG_FRAME_POINTER=y
-#CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE=4
-#CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE=y
+
 #
 # Clocks and Timers
 #
@@ -501,6 +498,7 @@ CONFIG_BOARD_INITTHREAD_PRIORITY=240
 CONFIG_SCHED_STARTHOOK=y
 CONFIG_SCHED_ATEXIT=y
 CONFIG_SCHED_ONEXIT=y
+CONFIG_SCHED_BACKTRACE=y
 
 #
 # Signal Numbers
@@ -1295,6 +1293,10 @@ CONFIG_MM_ASSERT_ON_FAIL=y
 # CONFIG_MM_DUMP_CORRPUTED_HEAP is not set
 CONFIG_MM_ALLOC_LARGE_FROM_BACK=y
 CONFIG_MM_LARGE_ALLOC_THRESHOLD=1048576
+CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE=3
+# CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE_SEQNO is not set
+# CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE_DEFAULT is not set
+CONFIG_MM_BACKTRACE_SKIP=3
 
 #
 # Work Queue Support
